  "result": "I fixed two bugs in `src/cart.js`, and `npm test` now passes (243 of 243).\n\n1. **Discount and tax were applied in the wrong order.** `total()` added tax first and then took off the discount. The comment in the code and the tests both say the discount comes off the pre-tax subtotal. The percent-discount tests didn't catch this because a percent discount and tax give the same total in either order. A fixed discount doesn't, so that test failed: it got 90 where 88 was expected.\n2. **A fixed discount could push the total below zero.** A $20 discount on a $5 item gave -14.5. The discounted subtotal is now held at a minimum of 0, as the comment says it should be.\n\nThe change is limited to `total()`:\n```js\nconst discounted = Math.max(0, applyDiscount(subtotal, discount));\nreturn round2(applyTax(discounted, taxRate));\n```\n\nI didn't touch `discount.js`, `tax.js` or the tests.",
